<figure class="l-body" id="fig-neuron-membrane">
  <pixi-neuron-membrane>
    <div class="scene" role="img" aria-label="A: a presynaptic spike travels to a synaptic channel in the neuron membrane, opening a conductance that can trigger sodium entry followed by potassium exit. Blue sodium and rose potassium ions cross through their respective channels. B above C: membrane voltage and inward-positive synaptic, sodium and potassium currents.">
      <p class="status" role="status">Loading neuron membrane…</p>
    </div>
    <div class="controls">
      <label><span>Capacitance <i>C</i><sub>m</sub></span><input data-capacitance type="range" min="0.5" max="2" step="0.1" value="1" /><output data-capacitance-value>1.0 μF/cm²</output></label>
      <label><span>Synapse</span><input data-weight type="range" min="0" max="0.6" step="0.05" value="0.2" /><output data-weight-value>0.20 mS/cm²</output></label>
      <label><span>Na channels</span><input data-sodium type="range" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="100" /><output data-sodium-value>100%</output></label>
      <label><span>K channels</span><input data-potassium type="range" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="100" /><output data-potassium-value>100%</output></label>
      <button type="button" data-restart disabled>Restart</button>
      <button type="button" data-pause disabled>Pause</button>
    </div>
    <noscript>An arriving presynaptic spike opens the synapse; its current raises membrane voltage and can recruit voltage-gated sodium channels. Sodium channels then inactivate and potassium exits, helping voltage return towards rest.</noscript>
  </pixi-neuron-membrane>
  <figcaption><strong>Figure 2.</strong> A presynaptic spike arrives and opens the amber synaptic channel. Its current can trigger sodium entry, followed by potassium exit, producing an action potential. The graphs show voltage and synaptic, sodium and potassium currents. Faint amber lines mark spike arrivals. Channel opening and ion motion are schematic; transmitter release, leak pathways and concentration changes are omitted.</figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
  import { deferMount } from '../../../site/src/lib/media-start';
  class NeuronMembrane extends HTMLElement {
    dispose?: () => void;
    connectedCallback() {
      this.dispose?.();
      this.dispose = deferMount(this, async () => (await import('./js/membrane.js')).mountMembrane, error => {
        console.error('Membrane animation could not start', error);
        const status = this.querySelector('.status');
        if (status) status.textContent = 'The animation could not start. Equations and the caption describe the model.';
      });
    }
    disconnectedCallback() { this.dispose?.(); this.dispose = undefined; }
  }
  if (!customElements.get('pixi-neuron-membrane')) customElements.define('pixi-neuron-membrane', NeuronMembrane);
</script>

<style>
  pixi-neuron-membrane { display: block; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #d6dfe7; border-radius: 12px; background: white; }
  .scene { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 124 / 36; position: relative; }
  .scene :global(canvas) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  .scene :global(.membrane-math-labels) { position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; color: #263343; }
  .scene :global(.membrane-math-labels sub) { font-size: .75em; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; position: relative; bottom: -.2em; }
  .status { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: grid; place-content: center; padding: 24px; margin: 0; text-align: center; }
  .controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(190px, 1fr) minmax(155px, 1fr) repeat(2, minmax(125px, 1fr)) auto auto; align-items: center; gap: 12px; overflow-x: auto; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px 4px 8px; border-top: 1px solid #eaf0f4; }
  .controls label { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; align-items: center; min-width: 0; gap: 8px; font: 13px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; color: #263343; }
  .controls label > span { white-space: nowrap; }
  .controls .mode { grid-template-columns: auto auto; }
  .actions { display: contents; }
  .controls > label input { grid-column: 1 / -1; grid-row: 2; }
  .controls > label output { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1; }
  input[type="range"] { width: 100%; min-width: 0; margin: 0; accent-color: #626b74; }
  output { min-width: 48px; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  button, select { border: 1px solid #cbd5df; border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 10px; background: #f5f7f9; color: #263343; font: 13px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; cursor: pointer; }
  button { min-width: 64px; }
  button:hover { background: #eaf0f4; }
  :is(input, button, select):focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #176d91; outline-offset: 3px; }
  button:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: default; }
  figcaption { margin-top: 12px; }
  @media (min-width: 1180px) {
    figure { grid-column: text-start / page-end; display: grid; grid-template-columns: subgrid; }
    pixi-neuron-membrane { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    figcaption { grid-column: text; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .scene { aspect-ratio: 62 / 36; }
  }
</style>
